Package: candled
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, adduser
Description: candle server for wincan: JSON candles over TLS, clients authorized by key
 candled serves candles (open, high, low, close, volume) from a collector's
 files or a SQLite database as JSON over HTTP.  It listens on the loopback
 address unless told otherwise, speaks TLS, and answers only the clients whose
 key it has been told, by the SHA-256 fingerprint of the client's own
 certificate (as an IRC bouncer does with certfp).  It also serves a modelled
 liquidation ladder for wincan's heat strip.
 .
 The settings are in /etc/candled.conf.  Make it let a wincan in with
 "candled --authorize SHA256:...".

Package: wincan-windows
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: candled
Description: wincan, the candle window for the Windows desktop, with its installer
 wincan.exe is a small frameless always-on-top candle chart window for Windows
 (candles, indicators, position profit and loss, a liquidation heat strip),
 fed by candled or any program that speaks the candle protocol.  This package
 holds the Windows program and a PowerShell installer for it, for use from a
 Debian or Ubuntu system, for example under WSL2:
 .
  powershell.exe -ExecutionPolicy Bypass \
    -File "$(wslpath -w /usr/share/wincan/windows/install.ps1)"
 .
 The program itself is not run or used on Linux.
